<h1 class="govuk-heading-l">Accessibility statement for the PT‑LIMS website</h1>

<p class="govuk-body">
    This accessibility statement applies to the Proficiency Testing Laboratory Information Management System (PT‑LIMS) website
    and associated online services. PT‑LIMS is provided and maintained by the Animal and Plant Health Agency (APHA).
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    PT‑LIMS is used to manage APHA’s proficiency testing schemes and to support laboratories in registering, submitting results,
    and accessing scheme information.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    We want as many people as possible to be able to use the PT‑LIMS website. For example, users should be able to:
</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Change colours, contrast levels and fonts using browser settings or assistive technology</li>
    <li>Zoom in up to 300% without text spilling off the screen</li>
    <li>Navigate most of the website using a keyboard</li>
    <li>Use screen readers (including the latest versions of NVDA) to read most content</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">
    We also aim to ensure that the language used across PT‑LIMS pages is clear and easy to understand.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    Guidance on making your device easier to use if you have a disability is available from AbilityNet.
    URL: <a class="govuk-link" href="https://mcmw.abilitynet.org.uk/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://mcmw.abilitynet.org.uk/ (opens in new tab)</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How accessible this website is</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">We know that parts of the PT‑LIMS website are not fully accessible:</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Text does not always reflow into a single column on narrow screens</li>
    <li>Line height and text spacing cannot be adjusted</li>
    <li>Some online forms within the system are difficult to navigate using only a keyboard</li>
    <li>
        There is currently no skip‑to‑content function for screen‑reader users. There is a navigate to main content CTA that can
        be invoke by hitting tab immediately a page is drawn
    </li>
</ul>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Feedback and contact information</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    If you need information from the PT‑LIMS website in a different format such as large print, easy read, audio recording or
    braille, please contact:
</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
    <li>Email: vetqas@apha.gov.uk</li>
    <li>Phone: +44 (0) 3000 600003</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">We will respond to your request within 2 working days.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Reporting accessibility problems</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    We are always working to improve accessibility across PT‑LIMS. If you find any issues not listed on this page, or believe we
    are not meeting legal accessibility requirements, please email
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:vetqas@apha.gov.uk">vetqas@apha.gov.uk</a>
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Enforcement procedure</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) enforces the accessibility regulations. If you are not satisfied with how we
    handle your complaint, you can contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service (EASS).
    URL: <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/ (opens in new tab)</a>.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    If you are based in Northern Ireland, contact the Equality Commission for Northern Ireland (ECNI).
    URL: <a class="govuk-link" href="https://www.equalityni.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://www.equalityni.org/ (opens in new tab)</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Contacting us by phone or visiting in person</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    We provide a text relay service for people who are deaf, hard of hearing or who have a speech impairment.<br>
    The VETQAS office is not equipped with audio induction loops. If you contact us before your visit, we can arrange a British
    Sign Language (BSL) interpreter.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">To contact us, refer to the Feedback and Contact Information section above.</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Technical information about this website’s accessibility</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    APHA is committed to ensuring PT‑LIMS is accessible in accordance with the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile
    Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Compliance status</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    This website is not fully compliant with WCAG 2.1 AA. Further investigations are ongoing to improve compliance.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Preparation of this accessibility statement</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
    This statement was prepared on 11<sup>th</sup> March 2026<br>
    It was last reviewed on 11<sup>th</sup> March 2026<br>
    The PT‑LIMS website was last tested in July 2025.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    Testing was carried out by the APHA internal accessibility test team. All pages were reviewed.
</p>
